From 06d90e63012507cb4d24417b351fb860c564bb5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 04:18:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 205/217] feat: water surfaces as traceable geometry - ocean
 ring and water volumes in the dynamic RT segment (CPU, decision 09 9.4)

Water was in no static soup at all: CheckCollectObjectsForVoxelization only queries
Brush / MovableBrush / Vegetation, and the ocean is procedural (COcean is a fake render
node that is never registered in the object tree). So a reflection ray could not see
water at any setting. Both halves are now emitted into the per frame DYN_MESH segment as
ordinary objects of the two level dynamic tree, inheriting its budget, its per object
quantisation and its stale tail zeroing.

Ocean: one camera centred quad grid at the water level, covering
+/- (e_svoTI_RT_MaxDistCam * e_svoTI_RT_DynObjDistRatio + e_svoTI_RT_MaxDistRay), split
e_svoTI_RT_WaterGrid cells per axis (default 4 = 32 triangles). The local mesh is cached
and rebuilt only when its radius or subdivision changes; a walking camera costs one
Matrix34. Gated on an existing COcean with a material, a valid GetWaterLevel(),
e_WaterOcean and OCR_NO_DRAW.

Water volumes: CWaterVolumeRenderNode's own surface mesh - exactly the vertices and
indices Render_JobEntry hands to CREWaterVolume - placed by the same matrix the render
object gets (identity, or m_parentEntityWorldTM when attached to an entity). Skipped when
hidden, pending delete, zero fog density (CE draws nothing either), out of the collection
radius or more than one ray length outside the frustum. Read through new read only
accessors on CWaterVolumeRenderNode; the cached BVH is re-validated every frame against a
(triangle count, first vertex) signature so an edited, moved or recycled node can never
keep a stale subtree. Every triangle is wound to face +Z, so water is single sided seen
from above and a hit from below is a back face the consumer rejects.

Material record: tag 4 (Water), matInfo1.y = 0.02 (water F0), matInfo1.z = 1.0
smoothness, matInfo2.xyz and extras+2.xyz = the fog colour (E3DPARAM_OCEANFOG_COLOR for
the ocean, m_fogColor x the time of day HDR multiplier for a volume), extras+2.w = the fog
density, extras+3.x = MatSpecColor (the sun specular scalar Water.cfx multiplies
CV_SunColor by), extras+3.y = ReflectionScale / ssrBGMultiplier, extras+3.z = the water
depth hint (e_svoTI_RT_WaterDepth, or the volume's own depth). No atlas slices are taken:
a water hit is shaded from the fog colour and the sky, not from an albedo map. Field table
and the GPU consumer contract in scene-notes/rt/reports/05c-water-cpu.md.

New cvars e_svoTI_RT_Water (1), e_svoTI_RT_WaterGrid (4), e_svoTI_RT_WaterDepth (5 m);
water is collected even with e_svoTI_RT_Dynamic 0 and the HUD line shows either.
"RT dyn:" gains "water N tris". e_svoTI_RT_SelfTest gains a water line: a synthetic ocean
ring and a volume quad through the real producer, the tag 4 record decoded back with the
consumer's own extractors, and 400 point pairs traced from above and from below - front
face from above, back face from below, 0 mismatches.

This commit also carries the four cvar registrations stage 4B (glossy reflections) could
not commit because this file was checked out here: e_svoTI_RT_GlossyMode,
e_svoTI_RT_GlossScale, e_svoTI_RT_TemporalFrames and the e_svoTI_RT_MinGloss 0.85 -> 0.5
default change, verbatim from reports/04b-glossy.md section 8.

Everything is behind e_svoTI_RT_Active; the native path is unchanged.
Cry3DEngine builds 0 error / 0 warning (Profile, bundled CMake 3.22). The engine was not
run and nothing was deployed.

